00:15:08.481 --> 00:15:10.025
have to worry about that, okay?

00:15:10.026 --> 00:15:11.990
So, let's think about
systems that create markets.

00:15:11.991 --> 00:15:14.130
Now, let me take just a very,

00:15:14.131 --> 00:15:16.140
very simple example to
try to bring this home.

00:15:16.141 --> 00:15:17.880
Recommendation systems to me were

00:15:17.881 --> 00:15:19.470
one of the more powerful
achievements in

00:15:19.471 --> 00:15:21.050
machine learning literature or

00:15:21.051 --> 00:15:22.660
machine learning history, okay?

00:15:22.661 --> 00:15:23.890
Before the current era,

00:15:23.891 --> 00:15:25.900
they took and lots of data
and they help people make

00:15:25.901 --> 00:15:28.120
decisions not just define
features and so on.

00:15:28.121 --> 00:15:29.620
They help people
make decisions, what

00:15:29.621 --> 00:15:31.535
books am I interested
in, and so on.

00:15:31.536 --> 00:15:33.390
The way they work
still to this day

00:15:33.391 --> 00:15:35.480
is that the decisions interact.

00:15:35.481 --> 00:15:39.380
So, if I come in to
the Amazon system today,

00:15:39.381 --> 00:15:42.120
they'll featurized me in
some way and they'll put

00:15:42.121 --> 00:15:43.150
me probably into a neural net

00:15:43.151 --> 00:15:44.990
these days and it will
output some recommendations.

00:15:44.991 --> 00:15:47.040
There are some books, or
some movies, or something else.

00:15:47.041 --> 00:15:48.635
Chris comes in later

00:15:48.636 --> 00:15:50.340
they will featurized Chris
and they will put him

00:15:50.341 --> 00:15:52.100
into the same neural net

00:15:52.101 --> 00:15:53.300
and they'll make
some recognition for him

00:15:53.301 --> 00:15:56.330
and those are totally
unrelated, right?

00:15:56.331 --> 00:15:57.960
Well, so if you're recommending
a movie that's fine.

00:15:57.961 --> 00:16:00.350
If they recommend the same movie
to me and to Chris and

00:16:00.351 --> 00:16:01.620
all of the rest of
you in the room

00:16:01.621 --> 00:16:03.170
or 100,000 people
that's no problem.

00:16:03.171 --> 00:16:05.475
They just bring the bits
to everybody. No problem.

00:16:05.476 --> 00:16:08.210
What if you recommend
the same book to everybody?

00:16:08.211 --> 00:16:10.380
Well, it's price
still not a problem,

00:16:10.381 --> 00:16:11.320
you can do what's called print on

00:16:11.321 --> 00:16:12.610
demand but getting into maybe

00:16:12.611 --> 00:16:13.940
100,000 copies of a book to

00:16:13.941 --> 00:16:15.760
all the people who were read,
Hey, that's not an easy.

00:16:15.761 --> 00:16:18.170
So it starts to become
just a little scarcity there.

00:16:18.171 --> 00:16:20.125
But now, what if you recommend,

00:16:20.126 --> 00:16:21.710
so you're trying to make

00:16:21.711 --> 00:16:23.200
a really good recommendations
for things like

00:16:23.201 --> 00:16:26.440
restaurant seats that not just
a bunch of advertisements,

00:16:26.441 --> 00:16:27.790
but actually really bids

00:16:27.791 --> 00:16:29.180
and link you up to
restaurants that

00:16:29.181 --> 00:16:30.570
you might want be
inserted into maybe at

00:16:30.571 --> 00:16:32.210
10% discounts and so on.

00:16:32.211 --> 00:16:34.130
Well, you can't recommend
the same restaurant seat

00:16:34.131 --> 00:16:36.185
to a hundred thousand
people, right?

00:16:36.186 --> 00:16:40.350
You'll create
congestion. Instead you

00:16:40.351 --> 00:16:41.310
have to load balance and you have

00:16:41.311 --> 00:16:42.280
to do this really with a market.

00:16:42.281 --> 00:16:43.550
You don't know what
people really want?

00:16:43.551 --> 00:16:45.000
What their preferences are?

00:16:45.001 --> 00:16:47.270
You don't want
the restaurants really have

00:16:47.271 --> 00:16:48.350
available so you can't just

00:16:48.351 --> 00:16:49.900
have the computer
know all of this.

00:16:49.901 --> 00:16:51.190
So you have to build
a market where

00:16:51.191 --> 00:16:52.840
the restaurants can bid on
the people and the people can

00:16:52.841 --> 00:16:58.315
accept or reject and start
to create two-sided market.

00:16:58.316 --> 00:17:00.050
What if I reckon, if I build

00:17:00.051 --> 00:17:01.260
a really good app for doing

00:17:01.261 --> 00:17:02.450
a how do you get to the airport?

00:17:02.451 --> 00:17:04.860
Path finding. If
just a small number

00:17:04.861 --> 00:17:06.010
of people are using
it no problem.

00:17:06.011 --> 00:17:07.345
But if everybody's using it,

00:17:07.346 --> 00:17:09.160
it might recommend
the same path to everybody

00:17:09.161 --> 00:17:10.970
and I create congestion and
that's already happening,

00:17:10.971 --> 00:17:12.310
you start to see that
happening with some of

00:17:12.311 --> 00:17:14.040
the apps and sort of
these when they get big.

00:17:14.041 --> 00:17:16.135
Well, you have to
think about that,

00:17:16.136 --> 00:17:19.045
we can't start creating
congestion in our lives.

00:17:19.046 --> 00:17:21.450
And here's another example,
is my favorite one,

00:17:21.451 --> 00:17:22.660
is like in China

00:17:22.661 --> 00:17:24.185
right now everybody's got
a little bit of money.

00:17:24.186 --> 00:17:25.390
And a thousand dollar,

00:17:25.391 --> 00:17:26.240
and they want to invest it

00:17:26.241 --> 00:17:27.170
for the first time in their life

00:17:27.171 --> 00:17:29.470
that might buy
a mutual fund or something.

00:17:29.471 --> 00:17:31.450
Well, if it's there
now their apps exists,

00:17:31.451 --> 00:17:33.690
which help people to make
their investment, right?

00:17:33.691 --> 00:17:35.985
Well, if that app suggests
200,000 people today

00:17:35.986 --> 00:17:38.605
to buy Microsoft stock,

00:17:38.606 --> 00:17:40.880
the stock's gonna go up
artificially and that's

00:17:40.881 --> 00:17:41.920
gonna move the market
and it's going

00:17:41.921 --> 00:17:43.020
to destabilize the market.

00:17:43.021 --> 00:17:46.070
You cannot do that.
Okay, all right,

00:17:46.071 --> 00:17:47.980
so I hope you get
the sense this is real.

00:17:47.981 --> 00:17:50.710
And at the same time,

00:17:50.711 --> 00:17:51.940
there's the classical problem

00:17:51.941 --> 00:17:52.780
of multiple decisions that's

00:17:52.781 --> 00:17:55.050
more statistical and these
are quite orthogonal,

00:17:55.051 --> 00:17:56.460
but you have to
solve both of them.

00:17:56.461 --> 00:17:58.495
And I hope you all kind of
know about how you make

00:17:58.496 --> 00:18:01.425
decisions now under uncertainty
not under scarcity.

00:18:01.426 --> 00:18:03.500
If you make decisions
under uncertainty,

00:18:03.501 --> 00:18:06.540
what you do is that you need
to make a decision here.

00:18:06.541 --> 00:18:07.805
Do jellybeans cause acne?

00:18:07.806 --> 00:18:09.330
Well, you randomly put half of

00:18:09.331 --> 00:18:11.470
your people and
you do an AB test,

00:18:11.471 --> 00:18:14.230
half the people go here,
they eat jelly beans.

00:18:14.231 --> 00:18:15.920
Half the people don't
eat jelly beans,

00:18:15.921 --> 00:18:17.690
and then you ask say
their skin condition

00:18:17.691 --> 00:18:22.385
six months later and probably
there'll be no effect.

00:18:22.386 --> 00:18:24.340
It will be within the error bars

00:18:24.341 --> 00:18:25.380
and you can get a P value,

00:18:25.381 --> 00:18:27.395
a quantitative assessment that

00:18:27.396 --> 00:18:29.280
you're making
a real decision based

00:18:29.281 --> 00:18:31.020
on the uncertainty
in this paradigm.

00:18:31.021 --> 00:18:33.540
But the people don't stop there,

00:18:33.541 --> 00:18:34.560
they don't just make one test.

00:18:34.561 --> 00:18:35.660
They say, "Well, it's
just a particular

00:18:35.661 --> 00:18:36.825
color that causes it."

00:18:36.826 --> 00:18:39.375
So now, they do
the AB test 100 times.

00:18:39.376 --> 00:18:40.880
All right, and now, by chance

00:18:40.881 --> 00:18:42.310
alone they put people
just happen to have

00:18:42.311 --> 00:18:44.750
bad skin condition and
the treatment condition

00:18:44.751 --> 00:18:46.410
and they will look like
they have bad condition

00:18:46.411 --> 00:18:47.670
after the test and it looks like,

00:18:47.671 --> 00:18:50.305
"Oh, I've made a discovery
green jelly beans cause acne."

00:18:50.306 --> 00:18:53.300
All right. Now, if you
had any statistics,

00:18:53.301 --> 00:18:54.760
you know about this, but
you probably don't know

00:18:54.761 --> 00:18:57.055
the solutions to this, okay?

00:18:57.056 --> 00:18:59.990
And the software I know of
no software that anybody is

00:18:59.991 --> 00:19:01.215
built in the machine
and ensure that

00:19:01.216 --> 00:19:03.130
puts in false discovery
rate control,

00:19:03.131 --> 00:19:05.690
which is kind of one of the
ways to deal with this.

00:19:05.691 --> 00:19:07.400
So you can deal with this.

00:19:07.401 --> 00:19:08.860
There's a notion called
false discovery rate

00:19:08.861 --> 00:19:09.925
and it's not an error rate.

00:19:09.926 --> 00:19:11.590
Error rate is
just a single number,

00:19:11.591 --> 00:19:13.580
all right. It's a ratio.

00:19:13.581 --> 00:19:15.220
There's a numerator
and denominator

00:19:15.221 --> 00:19:16.755
and you want that ratio
to be small,

00:19:16.756 --> 00:19:18.050
you can make it be
small by having

00:19:18.051 --> 00:19:19.790
the numerator small that's
a classical error rate

00:19:19.791 --> 00:19:23.150
going down or the new
denominator can be big, okay.

00:19:23.151 --> 00:19:25.120
And so you can control
the fraction of

00:19:25.121 --> 00:19:26.230
bad decisions in your entire

00:19:26.231 --> 00:19:27.915
lifetime not just on one day,

00:19:27.916 --> 00:19:29.800
not just the one decision
or a whole group of

00:19:29.801 --> 00:19:32.045
people that you can have
that fraction be controlled.

00:19:32.046 --> 00:19:34.355
Okay, so this is something
we've worked on at Berkeley.

00:19:34.356 --> 00:19:36.635
Here's a very recent paper,

00:19:36.636 --> 00:19:38.500
there's an algorithm
called DAgger.

00:19:38.501 --> 00:19:39.890
There is the algorithm,
you can put that in

00:19:39.891 --> 00:19:42.780
your software that will control
false discovery rate in

00:19:42.781 --> 00:19:45.900
an online setting
across lots and lots of

00:19:45.901 --> 00:19:48.200
decisions by making
the numerator and

00:19:48.201 --> 00:19:49.610
the denominator be
controlled and it

00:19:49.611 --> 00:19:51.320
doesn't require independence
and so on so forth.

00:19:51.321 --> 00:19:52.510
So this is really you
can real math with

00:19:52.511 --> 00:19:53.895
this kind of thing and
it should be done.

00:19:53.896 --> 00:19:56.240
Put that together with
the economic perspective and now

00:19:56.241 --> 00:19:59.540
there's wonderful research
challenges going forward.

